/*
:name: array_vs_packed_reset
:type: lec
*/
// PYROPE-vs-PYROPE group (README "Pyrope ↔ Pyrope variants"): this file is the
// REFERENCE, and every `array_vs_packed_reset_<N>.prp` beside it is LEC'd
// against it.
//
// THE CLAIM: `= 0` on a register ARRAY means the same thing it means on a
// scalar register -- the reset value. This is array_vs_packed_dyn with the
// `= nil` turned into `= 0` and nothing else changed, so a refutation here is
// about the RESET and cannot be about the read path (that group proves).
//
// It refutes today: on the whole-array `update` path, cgen emits the reset bus
// (`foo_data_rst`) and then never uses it -- the Memory cell's `reset` sink
// (graph/cell.cpp pid 14) is left unconnected, so the `always @(posedge)` block
// has no reset branch at all and the array holds whatever was written during
// reset. The packed spelling resets normally, which is the divergence.
pub mod top(we:u1, v:u16, raddr:u2) -> (rd:u4@[0]) {
  reg foo:[4]u4:[ordering="old"] = 0
  rd = foo[raddr]
  if we != 0 {
    foo = v
  }
}
